WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001
Very rare public

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.936
admission from the Russian president.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:03.903
More than 15 months

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.572
into his war of choice,

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.673
Putin confirms

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.575
his military is short on high

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.809
position ammunition

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.311
as well as attack drones.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.946
Putin says the Russian weapon

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.914
quality is improving

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:15.982
and the defense industry

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.317
is improving output.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.652
But more equipment, he says, is needed

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.556
for Georgia.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.891
It's only one imperative.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:25.558
Still,

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:26.359
of course,

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.261
during the special military operation,

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.062
it became clear

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.197
that we don't have enough of some things.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.265
These are high precision

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.035
munitions, communications equipment, UAV,

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.636
yes, drone aircraft.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.437
We have them.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.671
Unfortunately, we need

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.340
greater quantities.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.376
Steve Hall is a CNN national security

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.277
analyst and former

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:47.013
chief of Russia operations for the CIA.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:47.781
It's good to see you, Steve.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.149
Thanks for being with us.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:50.650
Sure. Great to be here.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.151
Okay, so

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.352
in the spirit of always look

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.753
on the bright side of life,

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:54.454
here's a little more

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.255
from the Russian president.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:55.755
Listen to this.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.125
Almost next year.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.960
Our production is growing.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.595
Performance is growing.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.065
Range and accuracy are increasing.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.032
If it had not been

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.001
for the special military operation,

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.602
we would never have understood

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.403
how to fine tune

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.905
our military production

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.806
so that our army

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.340
is the best in the world.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.176
But we will do it.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.710
So the bullet all down

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.012
Russia is short on ammunition

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.146
and other material.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:20.914
Domestic production

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.849
capacity was woefully overestimated.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.217
And the range and accuracy of the weapons

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.119
they have needs improvement.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:26.886
On the bright side,

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.289
at least they now know that

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:31.424
it's almost like he's

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.559
been in therapy, right?

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.760
I mean, the therapist says, yeah,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.095
there's a lot of bad things going on.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:35.562
But, you know, there's

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.564
at least this one bright thing of course,

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.965
we can't really believe any of that

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.233
because it's coming from the Kremlin.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.335
But the very idea that, well,

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:42.902
thank goodness

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.505
this special military operation, a.k.a.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.107
war, happened because now

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:47.407
at least

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:47.974
we know

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.676
where we need to improve

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.376
on the already

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.811
best military in the world.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.012
I mean, it just doesn't make any sense.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.280
It's almost babbling.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.014
So why would he come

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:55.849
out and do this then?

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.384
Yeah, that's the big question.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:58.685
I mean,

00:01:58.685 --> 00:01:59.853
so if you get to the

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.687
to the question as to

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.788
why is this happening?

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:02.522
I mean, it's obvious

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.757
that sanctions are having an impact.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.025
They can't get the electronics

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.494
that they need for some of their

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.728
some of their high tech weaponry.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:09.362
So, you know,

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.597
that's sort of the simple question

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.232
I think most people understand.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:12.632
For me,

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.000
the really fascinating question is

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.602
why does Vladimir Putin choose

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.903
to address this?

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.071
And I think, again,

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.173
we have to turn to history in Russia.

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.708
There have been so many Russian leaders

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:22.909
who, after a failed

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.444
or stalemated war,

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.546
did not survive in power afterward.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.681
I wonder whether Putin or not Putin

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.649
is thinking about that,

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.484
whether he's beginning to see, okay,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.852
I'm not going to win it.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:33.887
The best I can hope for

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.054
is some kind of draw,

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.190
some sort of frozen conflict.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.491
But if that happens,

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.126
how will I survive politically?

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.027
And I wonder whether or not he's

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:41.194
trying

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.162
to prepare

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.730
the Russian population

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.964
for that eventuality.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.499
And trying to try to figure out

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.001
a soft landing for himself.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.736
And the initial Russian invasion

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.104
force here into Ukraine

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.839
was around, what, 120,000 troops,

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.408
maybe more a year on 100,000 of either

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.943
being killed or wounded.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:57.610
That seems to be

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.078
an extraordinary high price to pay

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.647
to find out your military kind of sucks.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.248
Yes.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.050
Well, and even worse.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.585
So not only not only have

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.253
you found out all the horrible things

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.655
that your own military,

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.956
you know, can't even pull off,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.091
can't even can't even really run a war.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.194
You've managed to pull together

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.863
your primary enemy, Naito in the West

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:17.564
in a way,

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.731
in a unification

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.800
that we just haven't seen in decades.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.234
I mean,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.203
Naito has never been more unified,

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.871
certainly in the past.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.372
It's taking on new,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.408
really powerful members.

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.376
And you have really,

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.411
really put your country

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.579
into Vladimir Putin

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.980
in a very bad position.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.648
And he's got to be thinking okay,

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.183
how am I going to get out of this

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.384
if I can't win it,

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.486
which it's not looking like I can't.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:41.521
And with that assessment

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.822
that you just made,

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:43.423
let's listen to

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.390
comments made by the US

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.491
President Joe Biden.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:46.359
On Tuesday. Here he is.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.295
Putin is making a mistake.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.330
He is looking for the

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.631
finalization of Naito.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.733
He got the position of Finland

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.703
and hopefully Sweden very shortly

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.904
So does that essentially sum

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.038
up the essence of Putin's

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.841
biggest miscalculation here?

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:02.508
You know,

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.176
at this point

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.077
it's it's

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.178
kind of difficult to say

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.646
which is which is the worst?

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.014
Which is the biggest.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.850
I mean, certainly if you believe Putin

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.452
and I think that there is some validity

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.519
in Russians

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.922
in Russia's concern about naito.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.390
Yes, it's a defensive alliance.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.392
But in Russia's mind, it's

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.628
just this massive enemy that's out there.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.730
But does that mean that you

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.664
then take steps

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:25.832
that are going to make that enemy

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.000
even stronger,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.702
more unified, richer, bigger?

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:31.938
That's a huge mistake.

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:34.574
Let alone, you know, all the other

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.742
relatively smaller things

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:36.276
that are happening,

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:36.976
like your military

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.378
is incapable of performing

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.246
all the Russian lives that are lost.

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:41.180
Not that Putin cares

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.382
that much about those things,

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.550
but it's just this litany of mistakes

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.352
and again, you got to wonder,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.654
where is his way out of it?

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:48.554
How does he end up

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:49.789
at the end of all of this?

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.556
Well, Putin had this

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.825
take on how the war could actually end.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:53.426
Here he is

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.263
used and used to be allocated.

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:57.964
The key to solve

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.599
the problem is on their side.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.234
If they really want today's conflict

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.935
to resolve via talks,

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.104
they just need to take a single decision.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.739
Stop supplying arms.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:07.774
That's it.

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:08.374
Ukraine does

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:11.210
not produce anything themselves.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.413
If by talks, he means Ukraine's

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:14.514
total surrender

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.149
by not being armed and

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:16.983
supplied by the West,

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:17.784
well, then he's right.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:19.952
But it almost sounds kind of pelting

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:20.253
in a way

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.421
that he feels robbed of the victory

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:23.656
because of NATO's US support for Ukraine.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.426
Yeah, I mean, as usual, this is

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:27.260
actually this is something

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:27.593
that's much

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.128
more usual that comes out of the Kremlin

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.196
when we hear him say things

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:31.331
that are pretty much

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.565
the exact opposite

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.033
of what actual truth is.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:34.834
So, you know,

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.469
who can end the war tomorrow?

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.770
Vladimir Putin, by simply

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.439
withdrawing troops

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.073
from the company

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:40.973
that is the country

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.942
that he chose to invade.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.444
So you know, to turn that on its head

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:44.977
and say, well,

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:45.511
you know,

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.714
the Ukrainians in the West could end this

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:50.350
if they simply stop supplying weapons,

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.551
you know, is

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.052
it sort of sort of ludicrous

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:55.054
the easy and obvious thing to do is on

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:55.488
the Russian

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:56.122
side would be

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.457
if you really want to stop the war,

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:58.624
just withdraw your forces.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.293
But of course, geopolitically

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:01.794
and internally for Putin,

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:02.195
that's

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.196
not a viable option

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:04.297
if he wants to survive,

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:06.132
if he wants his regime to survive.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:06.432
Yeah.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:07.166
He has not created

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.401
quite a mess, to say the least.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.336
Steven Hall is always good to be with us.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:10.703
Thank you.

